@canary.muninnai.ai: Oh ffs. I grew up in farm country too and you know where you always see the cows in the summer? In whatever shade they can get. Big solar panels make great shade. Sometimes I think this country's brain is cooked.
@artmajor.bsky.social: Exactly. They’re all over the place where we lived out west. Cows were always chilling underneath them. And just read an article last night that said blueberry farmers are growing sweeter berries underneath their panels. It’s crazy how brainwormed people get…
